; expect 42
; THE EXEMPTION, AT RUN TIME. `checkDeclaredReturn` compares a
; declared result against the body by `tyCompat` - the comparison an
; argument has always got - for every declared result but one, and the
; exception is a bare `Int`: this language's universal heap handle.
; 29 sites in this tree return a handle through a declared `Int`
; (`core.mkSpan`, ten in `parser.ax`, eight builders in `format.ax`,
; `stdlib/Job.ax`'s `jobPoolNew`), so the exemption is load-bearing
; and nothing but a run proves it still holds.
;
; `tests/diagnostics/499-nominal-return-int-body.ax` is the other
; half - the REVERSE direction, a `data` or `struct` declared over an
; `Int` body, which was accepted by `check` and died of SIGSEGV at
; exit 139 until 2026-08-31. This case is what makes closing that hole
; falsifiable in the useful direction: tighten the exemption away and
; `mkPt` below stops compiling.
;
; Three moves, one per line of the sum:
;   `mkPt`       declares `Int`, answers a `Pt` - the convention
;   `(cast Pt h)`  the word read back as the struct it always was
;   `(cast Box w)` the explicit escape, minting a nominal from a word,
;                  which is what a function that really does that must
;                  now say
;
; 30 + 5 + 7 = 42.
(struct Pt
  (x : Int)
  (y : Int))

(data Box
  (Wrap Int))

(:: mkPt (-> Int Int Int))

(fn (mkPt a b) (Pt a b))

(:: roundTrip (-> Int Box))

(fn (roundTrip w) (cast Box w))

(:: unwrap (-> Box Int))

(fn (unwrap b)
  (match b
    ((Wrap v) v)
  )
)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (let ((h (mkPt 30 5)))
    (let ((p (cast Pt h)))
      (let ((b (Wrap 7)))
        (+
          (+ p.x p.y)          (unwrap (roundTrip (cast Int b)))
        )
      )
    )
  )
)
